":"dish","r":"dish/dagwood-sandwich","n":"Dagwood sandwich","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["A Dagwood sandwich is a tall, multilayered sandwich made with a variety of meats, cheeses, and condiments. It is named after Dagwood Bumstead, a central character in the comic strip Blondie, who is frequently illustrated making enormous sandwiches. According to Blondie scripter Dean Young, his father, Chic Young, began drawing the huge sandwiches in the comic strip in 1936."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-dagwood-sandwich"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dagwood_sandwich"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"]]},{"h":"More from American cuisine","links":[["Angel food cake","dish/angel-food-cake"],["Banana bread","dish/banana-bread"],["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"],["Barbecue sauce","dish/barbecue-sauce"],["Beer cake","dish/beer-cake"],["Better than sex cake","dish/better-than-sex-cake"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Blooming onion","dish/blooming-onion"],["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"],["Brunswick stew","dish/brunswick-stew"],["Buffalo wing","dish/buffalo-wing"],["Butter cake","dish/butter-cake"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Caramel apple","dish/caramel-apple"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Cheesesteak","dish/cheesesteak"],["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"],["Chicken nugget","dish/chicken-nugget"],["Chiffon cake","dish/chiffon-cake"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"],["Chimichanga","dish/chimichanga"],["Chow-chow (food)","dish/chow-chow-food"],["Chowder","dish/chowder"],["Cioppino","dish/cioppino"],["Clam chowder","dish/clam-chowder"],["Clam dip","dish/clam-dip"],["Club sandwich","dish/club-sandwich"],["Cobb salad","dish/cobb-salad"],["Cobbler (food)","dish/cobbler-food"],["Cook's Corner","dish/cook-s-corner"],["Crab cake","dish/crab-cake"],["Croffle","dish/croffle"],["Dagwood Bumstead","dish/dagwood-bumstead"],["Deep-dish pizza","dish/deep-dish-pizza"],["Desperation pie","dish/desperation-pie"],["Dirty rice","dish/dirty-rice"],["Donut hole","dish/donut-hole"],["Egg in the basket","dish/egg-in-the-basket"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"],["Fritter","dish/fritter"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/2/29/Dagwood_sandwich.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"I, EncycloPetey","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dagwood_sandwich.jpg"}},"dish/maekjeok":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/maekjeok","n":"Maekjeok","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Korean cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Maekjeok is a meat dish from Goguryeo. It is made by skewering seasoned pork and grilling it over a fire. Maekjeok is considered one of the precursors to bulgogi, a modern Korean meat dish."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-maekjeok"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maekjeok"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Korean cuisine","cuisine/korean-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Pork","ingredient/pork"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Maangchi","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"maangchi.com","note":"Maangchi's Korean recipe site and YouTube channel, one of the best known English sources for Korean cooking.","url":"https://www.maangchi.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Korean Bapsang","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"koreanbapsang.com","note":"Home-style Korean recipes from Hyosun, a Korean-American mom.","url":"https://www.koreanbapsang.com/category/recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Korean cuisine","links":[["Bap (rice dish)","dish/bap-rice-dish"],["Bibim-guksu","dish/bibim-guksu"],["Bibimbap","dish/bibimbap"],["Bosintang","dish/bosintang"],["Cheonggukjang","dish/cheonggukjang"],["Doenjang","dish/doenjang"],["Garak-guksu","dish/garak-guksu"],["Gochujang","dish/gochujang"],["Gopchang","dish/gopchang"],["Hwajeon","dish/hwajeon"],["Jijimi","dish/jijimi"],["Jokbal","dish/jokbal"],["Korean restaurant","dish/korean-restaurant"],["Maeun-tang","dish/maeun-tang"],["Makchang","dish/makchang"],["Mandu-guk","dish/mandu-guk"],["Mandu-gwa","dish/mandu-gwa"],["Meat jun","dish/meat-jun"],["Meju","dish/meju"],["Morkovcha","dish/morkovcha"],["Scorched rice","dish/scorched-rice"],["Seon (food)","dish/seon-food"],["Sungnyung","dish/sungnyung"],["Tteokbokki","dish/tteokbokki"],["Wakame","dish/wakame"],["Yakgwa","dish/yakgwa"],["Yukpo","dish/yukpo"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/21/Gwanaksan_Mountain_10_%2817337908936%29.jpg/500px-Gwanaksan_Mountain_10_%2817337908936%29.jpg","w":500,"h":304,"by":"Republic of Korea from Seoul, Republic of Korea","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gwanaksan_Mountain_10_(17337908936).jpg"}},"dish/tibok-tibok":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/tibok-tibok","n":"Tibok-tibok","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Kapampangan cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Tibok-tibok or carabao-milk pudding is a Pampangan dessert pudding made primarily from carabao (water buffalo) milk and ground soaked glutinous rice (galapóng). Originating in the Philippine province of Pampanga, it is especially popular in Cagayan. It has a soft jelly-like texture and is topped with latík (coconut milk curds) before serving. It is characteristically creamy white in color and has a delicate, sweet and slightly salty flavor. It is very similar to the more common maja blanca, albeit the latter is made with coconut milk and cornstarch."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-tibok-tibok"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tibok-tibok"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Kapampangan cuisine","cuisine/kapampangan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Kapampangan Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"kapampangankitchen.blogspot.com","note":"Blog dedicated to Kapampangan home recipes from Pampanga.","url":"https://kapampangankitchen.blogspot.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/68/07360jfFilipino_cuisine_foods_desserts_breads_Landmarks_Bulacanfvf_11.jpg/500px-07360jfFilipino_cuisine_foods_desserts_breads_Landmarks_Bulacanfvf_11.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Judgefloro","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:07360jfFilipino_cuisine_foods_desserts_breads_Landmarks_Bulacanfvf_11.jpg"}},"dish/turnip-cake":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/turnip-cake","n":"Turnip cake","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Cantonese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Radish cake, turnip cake or chai tow kway is a Chinese dish made of steamed rice flour and shredded daikon radish often served as dim sum.  It is traditionally called carrot cake in Singapore, but has no relation to European carrot cake.  Radish cake is commonly served in Cantonese and Teochew (Chaoshan) yum cha, usually cut into rectangular slices and sometimes pan-fried before serving. Each pan-fried cake has a thin crunchy layer on the outside from frying, and is soft on the inside, whereas the steamed version is soft all over.  Often served with a soya-oyster dipping sauce, it is one of the standard dishes found in the dim sum cuisine of China and is widely consumed in Indonesia, Singapore, Malaysia, Thailand, Taiwan and Vietnam, as well as in overseas Chinatown restaurants.  In Southeast Asia, the cakes are often chopped into smaller cubes and stir fried with additional ingredients."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-turnip-cake"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turnip_cake"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Cantonese cuisine","cuisine/cantonese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Daikon","ingredient/daikon"],["Daikon radish","ingredient/daikon-radish"],["Rice flour","ingredient/rice-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Made With Lau","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"madewithlau.com","note":"Family-run channel and site teaching Cantonese recipes from retired chef Daddy Lau.","url":"https://madewithlau.com","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"}]},{"h":"More from Cantonese cuisine","links":[["Cantonese restaurant","dish/cantonese-restaurant"],["Char siu","dish/char-siu"],["Har gow","dish/har-gow"],["Hong dou tang","dish/hong-dou-tang"],["Lap cheong","dish/lap-cheong"],["Rice noodle roll","dish/rice-noodle-roll"],["Siu mei","dish/siu-mei"],["Sweet and sour pork","dish/sweet-and-sour-pork"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/9b/Turnip_cake_at_Chua_Lam%27s_Dim_Sum_%2820201120174336%29.jpg/500px-Turnip_cake_at_Chua_Lam%27s_Dim_Sum_%2820201120174336%29.jpg","w":500,"h":344,"by":"N509FZ","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Turnip_cake_at_Chua_Lam's_Dim_Sum_(20201120174336).jpg"}}}